      "rationale": "This is the base equation of the mathematical summary countUpperFrom: scanning an empty IntSeq contributes zero uppercase vowels, independently of the parity flag.",
      "source_rule_id": "rule-10b63a2e2225cd457dcf51887aec2f5c265ce7e5117c82e30a96da4d69dce4ab",
      "start_line": 10,
      "text": "  rule countUpperFrom(.IntSeq, _:Bool) => 0"
    },
    {
      "attributes": [],
      "classification": "DEFINITION",
      "end_line": 16,
      "module": "COUNT-UPPER-VERIFICATION",
      "normalized_sha256": "dbe614f8b007441a5b97fefaac5825ae89bddf38faf17cc47420c3c905ada5d1",
      "rationale": "This is the structural recurrence defining countUpperFrom on a nonempty IntSeq: it adds the current character's conditional contribution and recurses on the tail with toggled parity.",
      "source_rule_id": "rule-dbe614f8b007441a5b97fefaac5825ae89bddf38faf17cc47420c3c905ada5d1",
      "start_line": 11,
      "text": "  rule countUpperFrom(iCons(C:Int, REST:IntSeq), EVEN:Bool)\n    => (#if EVEN andBool strContains(\n                       iCons(C, .IntSeq),\n                       strToCodes(\"AEIOU\"))\n        #then 1 #else 0 #fi)\n       +Int countUpperFrom(REST, notBool EVEN)"
    }
  ],
